{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dlin sequence</i>, the first term is a positive integer and each term after the first is calculated by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the previous term in the sequence, then doubling the result. For example, the first seven terms of the Dlin sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab734f0d1d149f394bac30bed297bd11a88a924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 10, 22, 46, 94, 190, 382$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The 5<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a848d885ca1b2262442b9e3a08d4390b52ccdac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> term in a Dlin sequence is 142. What are the 4<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a848d885ca1b2262442b9e3a08d4390b52ccdac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> and 6<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a848d885ca1b2262442b9e3a08d4390b52ccdac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> terms in the sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th term of the Dlin sequence. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb4b478b80e044421f327db7be89e19808c4038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a_{4} + 1) = a_{5} = 142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f31a42a23c637afe4b2ae5b8070b72ae9626d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4} + 1 = \\frac{142}{2} = 71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c39c97e619a718a9fcbb1cd326371cdc05ebfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4} = 71 - 1 = \\boxed{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f4776c0fa5ca2b7203992615b324d15d525922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a_{5} + 1) = 2(142 + 1) = a_{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67b8c34db72f2b7075099964bc45f1cbb4ca77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{6} = 2 \\times 143 = \\boxed{286}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"165\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012747\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 452/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2417/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.016      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    7.016      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36614:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012747 and revision id 282456. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}